# Docker only reads a .dockerignore from the build context's own root — since core/Dockerfile's
# build context is now the repo root (Frontend Phase 10, needed so it can COPY from /frontend
# too), this replaces relying on core/.dockerignore and ml-service/.dockerignore alone, which
# Docker would otherwise silently ignore for a repo-root context.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/npm-debug.log
.git
docs
PROMPTS.md
README.md
infra/osrm-data
infra/postgres_data
ml-service/models
